	<notes>
	      2012/11/19 [Tactrix] updated to include missing elements.
	      2024 [Analysis] Extended with additional verified tables from ROM analysis.
	      2025 [Ghidra H8/539F RE] Added TCU/Transmission category from decompilation of
	        tcu_shift_torque_mgmt @ 0x28fff and isr_sci3_eri @ 0x168e3.
	      2026-07 [Ghidra RE, session 10] STRUCTURAL FIX: tcu_shift_torque_mgmt was
	        discovered to have been mis-split by Ghidra's auto-analyzer into 4 separate
	        functions (a 2-byte inline data literal at ROM 0x29339-0x2933a, mistaken
	        for code, broke the boundary). It is genuinely ONE function spanning ROM
	        0x28fff-0x29c31, now renamed tcu_shift_torque_and_knock_mgmt, and it does
	        BOTH TCU shift torque coordination AND per-cylinder knock processing (the
	        latter previously mislabeled as an independent "knock_process_main" with
	        no findable caller). Fixing the boundary immediately surfaced the real
	        caller: isr_sci3_eri (COMPUTED_CALL @ ROM 0x169b1), matching this file's
	        pre-existing note above almost exactly. This also revises the session-3
	        "two independently-gated subsystems intentionally coordinating via shared
	        f3ac/f3ae" framing to "one function doing both jobs sequentially" - the
	        underlying RAM-register findings (f1f2 bit7 gate, EEC6/EEC8 octane chain,
	        etc.) remain valid, only the two-functions framing changes. Also confirmed
	        this session: the "TCU Shift Torque Cmd Lo/Hi - Per Gear" tables (below)
	        hold raw SCI3 protocol command bytes sent to the TCU, never used in any
	        arithmetic - their existing uint16 "units" scaling is correct as-is; small
	        values (1-2) are expected, not a data error. See logging.txt session 10.
	      Address mapping: XML address = file_offset + 0x10000
	      Axis RAM pointers: F0C0=RPM, F0C2=Load/MAP, F0C4=CoolantTempA(ADC),
	        F0C6=AirTemp(ADC), F0C8=CoolantTempB(ADC), F0CA=TimeAfterStart,
	        F0CE=ISCVDemand, F0D0=IAT_raw
	      TCU comms: SCI3 serial channel. ECU sends torque cut commands to TCU each crank pulse.
	        tcu_comms_state (RAM 0xf3d0): 0=idle, 1=rx_wait, 2=tx_active
	        tcu_shift_flags (RAM 0xf3cc): bit0=shift_in_progress, bit1=shift_done,
	          bit2=downshift, bit3=upshift, bit5=sport_mode, bit6=torque_cut_suppressed
	      NOTE on throttle_load_pct (RAM 0xf5de): this is computed as crank period delta
	        (T2GR1H - crank_angle_current) in isr_sci3_eri, NOT a TPS voltage reading.
	        It represents engine load derived from crank timing, not pedal position.
	      2026-07 [Ghidra RE, session 4] CONFIRMED: this ECU has no discrete "knock
	        retard degrees" value (same as Evo 4/5/6 - neither MUT profile exposes one).
	        Knock instead degrades Octane Level (MUT 0x27, RAM 0xEEC8/EEC9, starts at
	        0xFF=100%) via an intermediate hysteresis counter at RAM 0xEEC6, driven by
	        the knock-sum register (0xF3A2/F3A3). Full confirmed chain:
	          knock_process_main (0x2933b) -> writes knock sum F3A2/F3A3
	          -> knock_event_counter_update_eec6 (0x251c4): hysteresis vs ROM
	             thresholds 0xB3E/0xB40, drives EEC6 0-255 (up when clean, down
	             under sustained knock)
	          -> octane_level_compute_from_knock_counter (0x252d3): clamps/scales
	             EEC6, writes result to EEC8 = Octane Level
	        Octane Level is what blends between the High/Low-Octane Ignition Maps
	        and Knock Control/Octane Control Above Load tables already defined below -
	        the "retard" is implicit in that map blend, not a standalone logged
	        scalar. A second, independent writer (octane_level_init_or_force_from_
	        gear_table, 0x24e80) also sets EEC6/EEC8 from a per-gear ROM table at
	        0x2882 indexed by the current-gear-state variable f1fc, or forces 100%
	        under a separate condition flag (f0fe bit0) - gear-dependent
	        init/override, independent of the knock decay path. Both writers are
	        gated by RAM 0xf1f2 bit7 (same enable bit used for knock-to-TCU torque
	        coordination, see TCU comms note above and logging.txt session 3/4).
	        See logging.txt for full addresses, thresholds, and remaining open
	        threads (undecoded flag bits f1fe.3/f200.0/f0fe.0, ROM table 0x2882 not
	        yet cross-checked against the f1f0/f1f2/f1f4 per-gear config stride).
	      2026-08-13 [Claude]: removed 96 top-level table entries from this shared base
	        that duplicated (often with stale/pre-correction addresses) tables already
	        defined, hand-verified, and corrected in 21000011_1997-2001_RVR_X3_Mt__4g63t_.xml
	        (the only file that includes this base). Confirmed via full name-by-name
	        diff of both files' top-level table-name entries that every removed
	        name has a live, more-current definition in that ROM-specific file. Kept:
	        all scaling definitions (still relied on by both files), the SCALING_TABLE_*
	        holding-pen block (not part of the duplicate set), the Post Start Enrich Decay
	        Multiplier / Launch Control Speed Limit
	        tables (present here only, no ROM-specific override exists), and the TCU/MUT
	        sections (present here only). See RVRbase.xml history for the removed tables'
	        prior content if needed for reference.
	</notes>

