	<!-- 2026-08-14 [Ghidra] New scaling, TCU-specific. RVR is the only platform in this project
	     with TCU code, so this axis had no in-project precedent to match against existing
	     Load/Load16/Load8 scalings (all of which overshoot 100% on this axis's raw data).
	     Derived from TABLE_3D_000131FA_TCU's Axis2 (header 2d650, data 64,96,...,512):
	     x*100/512 gives a clean proportional 12.5,18.75,25,31.25,37.5,50,62.5,75,87.5,100%,
	     ending exactly at 100. Cross-checked 2026-08-14 against a real VR4 5-AT TCU ROM's
	     own "vr4_AT_base.xml" (external file, user-provided): its shift-point tables pair
	     VehicleSpeedAT with a Throttle Position axis using "Throttle%16" (x*100/255, 8-bit
	     domain, max raw 255), NOT a Load-style scaling - confirming the second axis on TCU
	     shift/pressure tables is throttle%, not engine Load, contrary to the Fuel-side f0c2
	     convention. This RVR axis's raw domain tops out at 512 (16-bit) rather than 255
	     (8-bit), so x*100/512 is the correctly-scaled equivalent for this table's storage
	     width. Renamed accordingly - see table comment below. -->
	<scaling name="TCULoad" units="%" toexpr="x*100/512" frexpr="x*512/100" format="%.2f" min="0" max="100" inc="1" storagetype="uint16" endian="big"/>
